- op: discuss  # 59fc
  at: '2026-10-18T21:39:03Z'  # 59fc
  by: agent  # 59fc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 59fc
  clock: 5  # 59fc
  nonce: 59fc  # 59fc
  message: "C++ HALF DONE in PR #1718 (dev e436ecd67f); C# half was PR #1717 (see notes above). cpp class/struct symbols now record meta virtual_members (declared virtual / override / final), override_members (override / final) and static_members, read from the class body, because an out-of-line definition repeats none of those keywords; inline in-class definitions also carry them as modifiers. type_hierarchy: cpp left NO_VIRTUAL_EXTENDS_LANGUAGES (now go, rust only); a cpp pair dispatches when the member is virtual in the parent or any ancestor (implicit virtual, walked over the one-hop parents with a visited set), or is the parent's pure virtual, or the child declares it override/final; never when static on either side. LIVE REPRO on dev e436ecd67f (hypergumbo run; shape.h: abstract Shape{virtual area()=0; describe(); static Create()}, Square:Shape{area() override; describe(); static Create()}, Plain{virtual f(){}}, Mid:Plain{}, Leaf:Mid{f(){} -- no keyword}; shape.cc: out-of-line Shape::describe/Create, Square::area/describe/Create): dispatches_to = exactly [Plain::f->Leaf::f, Shape::area->Square::area]. Before (dev e68bd7036d): Shape::describe->Square::describe and Shape::Create->Square::Create were emitted (abstract hop admitted every pair) and Plain::f->Leaf::f was absent (concrete hop denied). Production-path tests: test_type_hierarchy_linker.py::TestAbstractBaseDispatchEndToEnd::test_cpp_dispatch_is_decided_per_method and ::test_csharp_dispatch_is_decided_per_method; producer: hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_cpp_member_dispatch_modifiers.py. NOT RE-MEASURED: the 11 grpc static false positives and the 1894 other grpc edges the item cites -- grpc is a big-repo run, which the owner asked to clear first; the fixture reproduces the static shape. NOT CHECKED: same-name overloads with differing signatures still pair. OUTSTANDING: the owner confirmation this item requested re the WI-fahot objection (no edge schema was added; per-method symbol modifiers / class meta only); reopen if the owner rejects the design. A .h file in a repo with no .cc/.cpp sibling is read as C, so a header-only C++ library records nothing here -- not changed."  # 59fc
